cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code, data or the trained weights, please cite the paper as below."
title: "afferent-channel: code for State Beside the Text"
abstract: >-
  Code, experiment commands and paper for an afferent channel: a trained input
  path through which an agent harness or a game engine gives a language model its
  state (context fill, battery, a character's fear) beside every token, so the
  model can act on it mid-sentence.
type: software
